Z||000000||overlord||02-02-2000||05:09 PM||||i would like to get my baby painted this summer and started thinking about somethingt.<P>it is red with a lot of black decals and striping on it, would it be cheaper to get it painted the same red and redo all the decals or paint it entirely another solid color i.e. black..??<P>thanx in advance||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||02-02-2000||07:32 PM||||I have never done a color change job on a Fiero, but most shops will want to charge you at least a couple of hundred extra dollars for the job. It really would not be that hard to change the color because all the inner body parts are black and not body colored. I still would stay with the original color, but I aint you! So, make yourself happy, and make that Fiero look new again.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||02-02-2000||09:02 PM||||I don't know why you would want to paint a child, but if you must, how about one of the Day-Glo colors?  At least you'd be able to find him/her in a crowded mall.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mutfish||02-02-2000||11:06 PM||||....And be sure to use a non lead based paint....||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phaeton||02-03-2000||12:55 AM||||To recolor a car well takes more work and costs more, but can equal factory in look.<BR>You sit in it, you pick the color.  If you have access to a scale model paint it a few different colors, looks a lot different than a color swatch.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||02-03-2000||03:48 AM||||mutfish has a good point.  No reason to poison your kid.  Besides, poisoning is illegal in most states.<BR>Phaeton has a good point, too.  If you repaint your car the same color, generally all you need to do is the outside.  If you change colors, you have to do the inside of the doors, hood, trunk, etc.  More labor=more $$.||||reg||1
